Chapter 15
Values across borders; ethics, law and internal control
القيم عبر الحدود؛ الأخلاق والقانون والرقابة الداخلية
Orontes sells in four countries, buys from two more, and will shortly be asked to do something in one of them that would be unthinkable at home and is entirely normal there. This chapter is about that situation and two others like it.
Three outcomes meet here and they belong together. What happens to a company's values when it operates in places with different laws and different customs. How ethical behaviour differs from legal behaviour, which is the distinction the first question keeps running into. And how ethics and internal control depend on one another, which is where the second half of this book rejoins the first.
Figure F815-01 is your map.
Figure F815-01. Chapter 15 roadmap: values across borders, the gap between law and ethics, and the control environment that rests on it.
